WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.485
A private dashboard becomes valuable by combining selected inputs around a common

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:06.005
operational purpose.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:10.240
CCTV events may provide motion, object, tamper, or camera-health signals.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.865
Local vision AI can add descriptions or classifications,

00:00:12.865 --> 00:00:17.400
but its output should be treated as an imperfect observation that requires context.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.130
Endpoint tools may report malware, suspicious processes, policy violations,

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.270
or device isolation.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.340
Firewalls and network monitoring can contribute denied connections, unusual traffic,

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.809
new devices, and service changes.

00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:32.120
Authentication systems can show failed logins, new sessions, privilege changes,

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.400
and account lockouts.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.030
Vulnerability findings and asset inventory add exposure context.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.850
An alert involving an internet-facing,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.220
unpatched asset may deserve different priority than the same event on an isolated test

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.045
system.

00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:46.990
Inventory data should identify ownership, business purpose, location,

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:51.895
and criticality without becoming an uncontrolled repository of sensitive details.

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:55.230
Environmental sensors can report temperature, water, smoke, power, enclosure state,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.272
or other safety-relevant conditions.

00:00:57.272 --> 00:01:01.320
Manual notes and incident records capture observations that automated tools cannot.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.240
They also preserve the reasoning behind escalation, closure, and tuning decisions.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.575
Each source needs an owner, collection method, expected update interval,

00:01:08.575 --> 00:01:09.760
and failure indicator.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.150
The dashboard should distinguish no events from no data.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.900
A quiet sensor may be normal; a disconnected collector may create a dangerous blind spot.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:17.925
Collect purposefully.

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:20.905
Do not ingest every available field simply because it exists.

00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:24.440
Prefer the minimum data needed for detection, review, accountability,

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.848
and legitimate operations.

00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:28.790
Document source reliability, time synchronization, retention,

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:33.200
and access restrictions so combined data remains understandable and responsibly handled.
